---
title: "Start, check, and stop the BitChat daemon"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  s0: Daemon not running
  s1: Radio already in use
  s2: Waiting for command socket
  s3: Startup failed
  s4: Child exited before startup completed
  s5: Socket open, services starting
  s6: Services ready, waiting for the reply
  s7: Daemon running
  s8: Waiting for daemon exit
  s9: Daemon stopped
  s10: Daemon still shutting down
  s11: Daemon exited after the timeout
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: start while another session owns the radio
  s0 --> s2: start daemon
  s2 --> s3: startup fails or times out
  s2 --> s4: child exits
  s2 --> s5: open command socket
  s4 --> s3: startup fails or times out
  s5 --> s3: startup fails or times out
  s5 --> s4: child exits
  s5 --> s6: finish starting services
  s6 --> s3: startup fails or times out
  s6 --> s7: return startup result
  s7 --> s8: request stop
  s8 --> s9: daemon exits
  s8 --> s10: stop wait expires
  s10 --> s11: daemon exits
  s10 --> s9: daemon exits
